      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the patch stays, could the subject say \"4KB processes\" rather than \"compat\", and could the body say what fails without it on top of aosp/4368034?\n\nAs far as I can see, the body doesn\u0027t match the diff yet: inode keys already get the folio slice since aosp/4368034 (this patch takes it from the PTE instead of the VMA, and also uses it for anonymous shared keys); `get_user_pages_fast()` already rounds down to the process page, since `mm/gup.c` uses the per-mm `PAGE_MASK`, and the 4KB branch passes the unaligned `uaddr`; and no untagging or VMA lookup is added (the lookup this removes already untagged, and `get_user_pages_range()` untags on its own).",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "61d0ca67dfe5f1d9bf8d267fd5bc72d83603cc97",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "19e640d1_35616c83",
        "filename": "kernel/futex/core.c",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 642,
