      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T18:51:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the patch stays, I\u0027m worried this makes shared futexes in userfaultfd ranges fail in 4KB processes: `get_user_pages_range()` calls `__get_user_pages()` without `FOLL_UNLOCKABLE` (as I mentioned on aosp/4367611), so `handle_userfault()` returns `VM_FAULT_SIGBUS` and `FUTEX_WAIT` or `FUTEX_WAKE` on a missing page gets `-EFAULT`.\n\nAnonymous userfaultfd is allowed in 4KB processes (aosp/4312484 only gates the other memory types), and `get_user_pages_fast()` handles it today: fast GUP is off for 4KB mms (aosp/4312491), and its slow path passes `FOLL_UNLOCKABLE` to `__gup_longterm_locked()`. Fixing it in `gup_user_range()` would cover this caller too.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "61d0ca67dfe5f1d9bf8d267fd5bc72d83603cc97",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
