      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T18:51:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that the PTE that GUP pinned is the most direct source for the slice, but it looks like `span.offset` is the same value that aosp/4368034 already puts in inode keys. There, `p3s_futex_page_offset()` takes it from `vma_folio_offset()`, and every page cache or shmem folio that `get_futex_key()` keys by inode is mapped by a 4KB PTE at the slice that `vma_slice_offset()` gives its address (aosp/4366901, aosp/4368054, aosp/4368056).\n\nFor example, the alias case in `futex_shared_p3s.c` (aosp/4367986) maps file offset 0 at +4KB and at +8KB of a 16KB window. As far as I can see, both aliases get page 0, offset 0 of the inode with or without this patch, and so does a native process that maps the same byte. The only driver-selected slices at this point, from `vm_insert_page_slice()` (aosp/4367599) in `remap_vmalloc_range_partial()`, map vmalloc pages, which have no `-\u003emapping`, so `get_futex_key()` returns `-EFAULT` for them either way.\n\nIs there another case you hit? If so, could the futex test from aosp/4367986 move into this patch with that case? If not, would it be OK to drop this patch?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "61d0ca67dfe5f1d9bf8d267fd5bc72d83603cc97",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
